{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/214620-should-the-pale-brood-have-an-effect-on-mummies-spoilers-and-stuff","id":214620,"title":"Should the Pale Brood have an effect on Mummies? (Spoilers and stuff)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-31T07:11:02-07:00","id":214620,"title":"Should the Pale Brood have an effect on Mummies? (Spoilers and stuff)","content":"So, my Mummy campaign kicks off in two days' time. After going through character creation with one of my players we ended up deciding that the Pale Brood Uter was the perfect relic for her character (of course, I didn't let her read the background stuff about it being made by the Shan'iatu who would eventually become one of the Judges, or whatever it is that background is meant to refer to, we were solely looking at mechanical effects). I was mulling over the role this relic would play in the upcoming campaign, and a thought struck me. Would this relic work on Mummies?<br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm not asking from a balance perspective. The Pale Brood inflicts some kind of grievous harm on the target, usually fatal, but because the nature of it is entirely plot-determined and it doesn't even necessarily have to even kill the target I'm not particularly worried about it being used to snipe important NPCs or anything. It's pretty obvious that very few calamities would be able to kill a Mummy capable of sealing their flesh, that the Mummy would recover from harm far more quickly than a human, and that even if it does put them in the ground they just get right back up again after the Death Cycle. And of course I pick the when and how of the disaster, so it's hardly a reliable plan and I'm sure I'll be able to have it pan out in an interesting way no matter who the player decides to name.<br /> <br /> But the issue I'm struggling with is that the 22 Voices ask for the name of the target. Names are clearly important in Mummy. Irem was the Nameless Empire, the Nameless City, and at least five of the six gods we know about are Nameless (I can't remember if Azar is considered Nameless as well). Names clearly have power, and Arisen names are specifically mentioned to have been sealed in Duat when they underwent the Rite. All of this, keeping things Nameless and sealing Arisen names, seems to have been undertaken as some kind of protection against magical attack. I dunno, I'm just unsure on how to run this. I'm happy to go either way, in which case I'll generally go in favour of the one that gives the player more options. In that case, I suppose I would consider the act of naming the target to be just that, a mundane (under the circumstances) exchange.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any thoughts on the matter? I am honestly at a bit of a loss here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T12:49:18-07:00","id":214995,"title":"","content":"I think the Nameless aspects refer to the true name (a la name magic) while the Brood, iirc, dont have that strict of a requirement. Ive run into similar problems in my crossovers with Mage, changeling, and to a degree, demon. Id say know the legendary title of that mummy would be enough to target them, as thats what mummies use in place of a true name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T14:06:50-07:00","id":215045,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the brood doesn't call for a true name, it just needs a designator so it can find the target. Look at Familiar Face (The affinity) and assume that any name that you could intuit through that affinity will probably work to target the brood","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T06:35:15-07:00","id":215816,"title":"","content":"Sounds about right. It would have been interesting to think if the 22 Voices were what caused the Shan'iatu to decide that they couldn't afford to name their city or empire. It's more likely though that when the Book of the Deceived comes out we'll see that it had something to do with the kind of magic they were practicing at the time, and fears that it might be turned against them or something.<br /> <br /> Anywho, cheers for the help guys. Helped make my mind up for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T08:24:45-07:00","id":215892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/214620-should-the-pale-brood-have-an-effect-on-mummies-spoilers-and-stuff?p=215816#post215816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds about right. It would have been interesting to think if the 22 Voices were what caused the Shan'iatu to decide that they couldn't afford to name their city or empire. It's more likely though that when the Book of the Deceived comes out we'll see that it had something to do with the kind of magic they were practicing at the time, and fears that it might be turned against them or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually say in the corebook. Nothing with a Name can be truly eternal. The same reason all the gods are nameless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}